The cards are saved as 10, 20, 30, 40. While card 20 (position 1) is being deleted, the last card is moved into the empty place. What is printed when the code runs?

```
byte kart[4] = {10, 20, 30, 40};
byte n = 4;
int sira = 1;
kart[sira] = kart[n - 1];
n--;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
  Serial.print(kart[i]);
  Serial.print(' ');
}
```

